at one of many different crime scenes  across several communities a search for  clues for a motive  for some answers  this is the home of wes peterson in his  late 70s he was stabbed inside while his  grandson hid in the cellar  his neighbors who know they could so  easily have been victims too  remembered a kind popular friend  i don't understand why they would target  someone like him anyway  because he was just a poor helpless  little man and  everybody cared about him because  that's the way he was he cared about  everybody else and they cared about him  the investigation into multiple  stabbings and the manhunt which followed  has been one of the biggest in canadian  police history it took a dramatic turn  late yesterday when one of the two  suspects was found dead the deceased is  damian sanderson  his body was located outdoors in a  heavily grassed area in proximity to a  house that was being examined  we can confirm he has visible injuries  these injuries are not believed to be  self-inflicted at this point  damien's brother miles sanderson remains  on the run police have now confirmed  that they have been looking for him  since may  he'd been released on probation from a  five-year sentence for assault and  robbery  it was at 5 40 on sunday morning when  the police received the first 9-1-1 call  the unfolding horror was soon clear with  multiple calls in minutes from over a  wide area  the province of saskatchewan lies in the  centre of canada the largely indigenous  communities targeted are small and  isolated from each other  the police identified 13 crime scenes at  several locations in the james smith  cree nation indigenous community and the  smaller village of weldon half an hour  drive to the south west  among the victims to be named lana head  a mother and a grandmother my thoughts  and the thoughts of all canadians are  with those who've lost loved ones  and with those who are injured  this kind of violence  or any kind of violence  has no place in our country the  investigation now has multiple strands  the manhunt and the motive are key some  victims appear to have been specifically  targeted  others were stabbed at random  it will take a lot for these communities  to begin to recover from such an  extraordinary series of attacks  mark stone sky news
 

